course: dictionary
lesson: 15211
title: Sensational
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sensational is an adjective. It describes something very exciting, surprising or amazing. «The fireworks were sensational.» People gasped and cheered, so you can tell the fireworks were amazing.
explain: In sport, a sensational goal makes the crowd go wild. «She scored a sensational goal in the last minute.» Here sensational is praise: the goal was amazing.
explain: Be careful with news. Sometimes a headline is sensational because it is made to shock people more than the facts deserve. «SENSATIONAL SECRET FOUND!» may sound exciting, but a good reader checks the real facts before believing it.
fact: Sensational means very exciting, surprising or amazing.
fact: In everyday talk, «you look sensational» means you look extremely good.
fact: Sensational news can shock people more than the facts deserve, so always check it.
fact: A sensational headline is written to grab attention.
fact: Useful phrases: «a sensational win», «sensational news», «sensational headlines».
exercise: «The crowd roared after her sensational goal.» What does sensational mean here? | Sad and sorry | Small and quiet | Boring and slow | *Amazing and very exciting
exercise: «The headline said: SENSATIONAL SECRET FOUND!» Why should a reader check the facts? | *Sensational headlines can exaggerate to grab attention | Capital letters show the news is wrong | Facts are never needed in news | Headlines always tell the whole truth
exercise: Which sentence uses sensational as praise? | *«You look sensational in that jacket.» | «The bus was late again.» | «The shop was closed on Sunday.»
test: «The magician's trick was sensational, and the whole room gasped.» What does sensational mean? | *Very exciting and amazing | Very wet | Very late | Very quiet and dull
test: «The newspaper printed a sensational story, but the facts were very small.» What does this tell you? | The story was exactly true | *The story was made to shock people more than the facts deserve | The story was about the weather | The story was too short to read
exam: Which sentence uses sensational in the same way as «a sensational goal»? | «The grass was wet this morning.» | *«The concert was sensational and everyone danced.» | «The bus was late again.» | «The dog was sleeping under the table.»
